    "message": "Year-to-date revenue grew 32.8% over the same period last year, but same-store revenue grew only 7.7%.\n\n- **Periods compared:** 1 January to 30 September in 2026 and in 2025. The latest order is from 29 October 2026, so October isn't complete and I left it out.\n- **Revenue basis:** pre-tax sales, the sum of order subtotals divided by 100 to get dollars.\n- **Headline:** $3,155,903 in 2025 versus $4,192,519 in 2026.\n- **Same-store:** $3,033,611 versus $3,267,590. This counts only stores that opened before 1 January 2025: Philadelphia, Brooklyn, Chicago and San Francisco.\n- **Why the two differ:** most of the headline growth comes from two newer stores. New Orleans opened in May 2025, so this is the first time it counts for the full period. Los Angeles opened in November 2025, so it had no sales in last year's period.\n\nThe store opening dates in the database are later than the ones in the business rules (for example, Philadelphia shows 31 October 2022 instead of September 2022). I used the database dates. The same four stores qualify as comparable under either set of dates."
